      "source": [
        "## 4. Prepare Features and Target\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Features (`X`)**: `Income`, `Credit_Score`, `Loan_Amount`, `DTI_Ratio`, `Employment_Status`\n",
        "* **Target (`y`)**: `Approval`, label-encoded as `Rejected = 0`, `Approved = 1` (the target is **not** one-hot encoded).\n",
        "* **`Employment_Status`** is one-hot encoded, but *inside the pipeline* (Section 6) so that the encoder is fitted on training data only.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why is `Text` excluded?** `Text` is free-form natural language (the stated purpose of the loan). Using it would require a separate NLP feature-extraction step (e.g. TF-IDF) and a different modelling workflow. The initial goal is a clean comparison of two models on *structured* data, so `Text` is left out for now. It is a candidate for future work; whether it carries any predictive signal has not been tested here."
      ]
    },
