      "source": [
        "## 5. Train/Test Split\n",
        "\n",
        "An 80/20 split with `random_state=42`.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why `stratify=y`?** Only ≈ 16 % of applications are *Approved*. A plain random split could, by chance, put noticeably more or fewer *Approved* rows in the test set, making metrics unstable and not comparable. Stratification keeps the class proportions (≈ 84 / 16) the same in both the training and the test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "The test set is split off **once, now**, and is not used for any tuning or model selection."
      ]
    },
