      "source": [
        "## 6. Preprocessing with a Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "Preprocessing lives **inside** scikit-learn pipelines, so it is fitted only on the data passed to `.fit()` (the training data, or the training folds during cross-validation). This avoids leakage.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Numeric features | `Employment_Status` |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Logistic Regression | `StandardScaler` | One-hot encoding |\n",
        "| Random Forest | passed through unscaled (trees are scale-invariant) | One-hot encoding |\n",
        "\n",
        "`handle_unknown=\"ignore\"` makes the encoder robust to unseen categories at prediction time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "id": "0ca8e7dc",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-24T11:06:03.758210Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-24T11:06:03.757837Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-24T11:06:03.762124Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-24T11:06:03.761463Z"
        },
        "id": "0ca8e7dc"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def build_preprocessor(scale_numeric):\n",
        "    numeric_step = StandardScaler() if scale_numeric else \"passthrough\"\n",
        "    return ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "        transformers=[\n",
        "            (\"num\", numeric_step, NUMERIC_FEATURES),\n",
        "            (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=False), CATEGORICAL_FEATURES),\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        verbose_feature_names_out=False,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_logreg_pipeline(class_weight=None):\n",
        "    return Pipeline([\n",
        "        (\"preprocessor\", build_preprocessor(scale_numeric=True)),\n",
        "        (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, class_weight=class_weight)),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_rf_pipeline(n_estimators=300, n_jobs=-1, **rf_params):\n",
        "    return Pipeline([\n",
        "        (\"preprocessor\", build_preprocessor(scale_numeric=False)),\n",
        "        (\"model\", RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=n_estimators, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=n_jobs, **rf_params)),\n",
        "    ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "70954386",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "70954386"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Addressing Class Imbalance\n",
        "\n",
        "With ≈ 84 % *Rejected*, a model that always predicts *Rejected* would already score ≈ 84 % accuracy while being useless. So accuracy alone cannot be the only guide.\n",
        "\n",
        "We compare the **normal** and **`class_weight=\"balanced\"`** versions of both models using **5-fold stratified cross-validation on the training set only** (the test set is untouched). `class_weight=\"balanced\"` re-weights the loss so mistakes on the rare *Approved* class count more.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Selection rule (decided before looking at results):** for each model family, pick the variant with the higher mean cross-validated **F1-score** of the *Approved* class, because F1 balances precision and recall on the minority class.\n",
        "\n",
        "SMOTE is deliberately **not** used: class weights already address the imbalance without creating synthetic rows."
      ]
    },
