      "source": [
        "## 10. Model Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "Both final models are evaluated **once** on the held-out test set with Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score, a confusion matrix and a classification report. Precision, Recall and F1 refer to the **Approved** class (label 1).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why accuracy alone is not enough here:**\n",
        "* A model that predicts *Rejected* for everybody reaches ≈ 84 % accuracy but finds **zero** approved applicants. A `DummyClassifier` is included as a reference to show this.\n",
        "* *Precision* answers: of the applications predicted *Approved*, how many really were?\n",
        "* *Recall* answers: of the truly *Approved* applications, how many did we find?\n",
        "* *F1* is the harmonic mean of the two."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 12,
      "id": "7d199442",
      "metadata": {
