        "## 14. Logistic Regression Coefficients\n",
        "\n",
        "Numeric features were standardized, so their coefficients are on a comparable scale (per one standard deviation). One-hot columns are 0/1.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Positive coefficient** → raises the model's log-odds of *Approved*.\n",
        "* **Negative coefficient** → lowers the model's log-odds of *Approved*.\n",
        "\n",
        "These describe the fitted model, not causal effects. The two `Employment_Status` columns are mirror images of each other, so their coefficients are partly redundant (they have opposite signs)."
      ]
    },
