      "source": [
        "## 15. Probability / Threshold Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "Classifiers output a probability; the default rule \"predict *Approved* if probability ≥ 0.5\" is only one choice. Raising the threshold usually increases precision and lowers recall; lowering it does the opposite.\n",
        "\n",
        "To avoid touching the test set, this analysis uses **out-of-fold predicted probabilities on the training data** (each row is scored by a model that did not see it). The main results in this notebook **remain at the default 0.5 threshold**. Nothing below is applied to the test set."
      ]
    },
