      "source": [
        "### Reading the threshold analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Logistic Regression:** raising the threshold trades recall for precision and lowering it does the reverse. In the out-of-fold training data its F1 was slightly higher at thresholds around 0.3 than at 0.5. That is an observation for illustration only. **No threshold was tuned or applied**, and the reported test results all use 0.5.\n",
        "* **Random Forest:** precision and recall stay high across a wide range of thresholds, and F1 peaks at about 0.5. This suggests the forest separates the two classes with high confidence.\n",
        "* If a threshold were ever changed for real use, it should be chosen on validation data (or out-of-fold predictions like these) according to the cost of each error type, then checked once on the test set."
      ]
